// 'Veach, MIS' — Benedikt Bitterli (CC0, public domain; crediting the
// artist encouraged). The classic multiple-importance-sampling plates:
// four metal bars of stepped roughness under light sources of stepped
// size. Official pbrt-v4 export from
// https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/ — `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh
// veach-mis` materializes the source; this RON was bootstrapped once by
// `cenote-cli import sources/bitterli/veach-mis/scene-v4.pbrt` and is the
// source of truth — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it. The
// geometry is inline in the source pbrt, so it is inline here too: the
// RON is self-contained.
//
// Import fidelity: exact in effect — the importer averages pbrt's u/v
// roughness axes (4 warnings at import), but every pair in this scene is
// equal-axis, so the average is the identity. max_bounces 3 is the
// source's own maxdepth, kept: the MIS comparison is a direct-lighting
// test. Anisotropic-roughness support would silence the warnings without
// changing a pixel.
